/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 138 0 R
/E (This thesis investigates the structural and evidentiary asymmetries within the English statutory planning system. It deploys a federated spatial data pipeline that programmatically cross-references contested planning sites against 65 live open-government spatial layers, complementing existing qualitative case-study research in this field. The empirical foundation is a locked, audited cohort of N = 652 contested planning sites, drawn from a gross harvest of N = 852 grassroots campaigns via a seven-stage sample-flow attrition funnel followed by collapsing repeat submissions of the same site.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [14]
>>
