540 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 146 0 R
/T (This chapter documents the federated software architecture executing 33 parallel asynchronous HTTP requests against 65+ live open-government spatial layers. A key technical challenge is the coordinate projection gap: statutory UK environmental constraints are natively indexed in British National Grid \(EPSG:27700\), whereas standard web APIs output WGS84 \(EPSG:4326\). Passing WGS84 coordinates directly into a statutory endpoint casts query points into the Atlantic Ocean, producing false negatives across the entire cohort. An in-memory geodetic engine was built in pure TypeScript to resolve this.)
/E (This chapter documents the federated software architecture executing 33 parallel asynchronous HTTP requests against 65+ live open-government spatial layers. A key technical challenge is the coordinate projection gap: statutory UK environmental constraints are natively indexed in British National Grid \(EPSG:27700\), whereas standard web APIs output WGS84 \(EPSG:4326\). Passing WGS84 coordinates directly into a statutory endpoint casts query points into the Atlantic Ocean, producing false negatives across the entire cohort. An in-memory geodetic engine was built in pure TypeScript to resolve this.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
541 0 obj
