<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (The Flipped Archetype Finding \(Track E2 & E3\): Strategic Residential Sprawl is under-represented in data deserts: 28.5% \(97/340\) vs. 42.1% \(126/299\) for all other archetypes \(OR = 0.55 [0.39, 0.76], Fisher's p = 0.00035\). Data deserts concentrate instead in utility-scale energy \(63.6%\) and freight logistics depots \(47.1%\). Developer-owned sprawl link test \(Track E3\): OR = 0.42 [0.09, 1.95], Fisher's p = 0.35 \(clean inconclusive null, provisional pending the E1 classification for 111 new v6 sites\). The "developers target data deserts" hypothesis is refuted for residential development. Level 2 \(statistical association\).)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
